{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.bound_clears_K_1p1e7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.bound_clears_K_1p1e7","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaLipschitzObstruction.lean#L207-L212","doc":"`K = 1.1 × 10⁷` finally clears the bound, so the exclusion is sharp: the\nforced Lipschitz constant lies between `10⁷` and `1.1 × 10⁷`.  Recorded so the\nresult is a bracket, not a one-sided \"at least\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.bound_excludes_K_1e7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.bound_excludes_K_1e7","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaLipschitzObstruction.lean#L199-L205","doc":"**`K = 10⁷` is STILL excluded** (bound `4.56e-2` vs measured `4.9e-2`).\n\nWorth stating: a first draft of this file asserted the opposite, guessing `10⁷`\nwould clear.  It does not — the threshold is `≈ 1.07e7`, and the guess was wrong\nby that factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.bound_excludes_K_1e6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.bound_excludes_K_1e6","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaLipschitzObstruction.lean#L195-L197","doc":"`K = 10⁶` is still excluded — the bound reaches only `4.6e-3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.bound_excludes_K_1e3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.bound_excludes_K_1e3","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaLipschitzObstruction.lean#L190-L193","doc":"`K = 10³` is excluded: the bound is `4.6e-6`, four orders below the measured\n`0.049`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.lipschitz_constant_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.lipschitz_constant_ge","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaLipschitzObstruction.lean#L169-L180","doc":"**The Lipschitz constant is bounded below.**  Rearranged division-free:\ngiven the measured variation, any valid `K` satisfies this.  With\n`|Δq| ≈ 1.3e-8` and `|S₁ − S₂| ≈ 4.9e-2` it is what forces `K ~ 10⁷`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.not_lipschitz_of_s_variation_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.not_lipschitz_of_s_variation_gt","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaLipschitzObstruction.lean#L154-L167","doc":"**The exclusion, contrapositive.**  If the measured S-variation EXCEEDS the\nLipschitz bound, no such `K` works — the candidate ϑ is excluded.\n\nThis is the form to apply as an up-front filter: compute the bound for the\ncandidate's Lipschitz constant, compare against the measured `|S₁ − S₂|`, and\ndiscard on failure without ever evaluating the candidate's value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.s_variation_le_of_lipschitz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaLipschitzObstruction.s_variation_le_of_lipschitz","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaLipschitzObstruction.lean#L117-L152","doc":"**A Lipschitz ϑ bounds the S-variation.**\n\nIf the channel `S = A·κ·(L − ϑ²)` holds at two substrate points, and ϑ is\n`K`-Lipschitz between them, then `S` cannot move further than the bound.\n\nNo division, no differentiability: Lipschitz is all that is assumed, and every\nsmooth geometric quantity is Lipschitz on a compact interval. ","signatureChunk":0}]}